course: dictionary
lesson: 8557
title: The scapegoat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scapegoat is a person or group blamed for something bad that is not really their fault, so that others escape the blame. Look for clues in the words around it. «He was made a scapegoat for the broken window» tells you he was blamed, and the word «made» hints that it was unfair.
explain: Scapegoat can also be a verb. «The manager tried to scapegoat the new worker» means the manager unfairly blamed the new worker. Use the swap check: put your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word has an old story behind it. In the Bible, on the Day of Atonement, the priest put the people's sins on a goat and sent it into the desert. The goat carried the blame away, and that is where the idea of blaming someone else began.
fact: A scapegoat is a person or group blamed for something bad that is not really their fault.
fact: Scapegoating is unfair, because the person blamed did not do the wrong thing.
fact: In history, whole groups were wrongly used as scapegoats, such as Jews in Nazi Germany.
fact: As a verb, «scapegoat» means to unfairly blame someone this way.
fact: «Blaming someone who cannot speak up, like a pet or a baby, is extra unfair; a "scapegoat" is someone blamed for other people's mistakes.»
exercise: «He was made the scapegoat for the broken window, though he never touched it.» What does scapegoat mean here? | A player who scores every goal | A goat that lives in the school garden | *A person blamed for something that is not really their fault | The one who really broke the window
exercise: «The manager tried to scapegoat the new worker for the lost money.» What does scapegoat mean as a verb? | To find the lost money | To keep a secret safe | To thank someone for their help | *To unfairly blame someone this way
exercise: Which sentence shows scapegoating? | Ravi put the rubbish in the bin | Ravi and Sam both said sorry for the mess | *Ravi was blamed for the mess, although Sam had made it | Ravi cleaned up the mess and thanked everyone
test: Why is it extra unfair to blame a pet for a mess? | Because pets are too small to be seen | Because pets are always clean | Because pets never make a mess | *Because the pet cannot speak up to defend itself
test: In the Bible, what did the priest send into the desert on the Day of Atonement? | A lamb carrying a golden bell | A bird carrying a letter | *A goat carrying the people's sins | A goat carrying food for the poor
exam: In «The teacher used Ellie as a scapegoat», what does scapegoat mean? | A pet that the teacher looks after | A teacher's helper who fetches books | Someone who is always chosen first for games | *Someone blamed unfairly for other people's mistakes
